WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:01:00.030
<b>Summary of previous episodes</b>

00:00:02.320 --> 00:00:06.750
<i>Last time on </i>Frankenstein Family<i>...</i>

00:00:07.730 --> 00:00:12.320
<i>My genius planning and 
my sisters' special powers</i>

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:17.120
<i>allowed us to complete our mission 
and retrieve the research data.</i>

00:00:18.090 --> 00:00:24.710
<i>We ran into a little trouble, but when our 
family works together, we can do anything!</i>

00:00:26.630 --> 00:00:30.840
<i>But when I think about how the days 
we spent together in that facility</i>

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:33.260
<i>are behind us for good,</i>

00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:36.290
<i>it makes me feel a little bit low...</i>

00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:44.190
<i>And Yu Kaito-san, the landlord, 
was waiting for us when we got back...</i>

00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:48.690
<i>I'm still not sure if we can trust adults,</i>

00:00:48.690 --> 00:00:53.320
<i>but this guy's okay... I think?</i>

00:01:16.930 --> 00:01:23.210
<b>Frankenstein Family</b>

00:02:37.530 --> 00:02:42.490
<b>#6: Monster</b>

00:03:01.660 --> 00:03:02.970
Morning, Tanisu.

00:03:02.970 --> 00:03:04.600
Good morning, Tani-chan.

00:03:05.420 --> 00:03:07.330
He's still half-asleep.

00:03:09.370 --> 00:03:11.820
Wash up, then eat with us.

00:03:15.080 --> 00:03:19.090
<i>We'll be living with the 
landlord starting today.</i>

00:03:24.590 --> 00:03:28.100
It ain't as good as bugs, 
but it ain't bad, either.

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:31.430
It seems sufficiently nutritious!

00:03:32.470 --> 00:03:33.350
Tasty!

00:03:34.060 --> 00:03:36.570
I've lost all interest in dog food.

00:03:37.230 --> 00:03:39.910
What kind of life have you kids been living?

00:03:40.950 --> 00:03:42.770
I suppose you had a nice rest?

00:03:43.560 --> 00:03:46.580
Yeah, I haven't had a bed in so long.

00:03:47.140 --> 00:03:50.580
Usually, Snow-niisan and I are
 stuck sleeping on the floor.

00:03:50.580 --> 00:03:53.580
<i>Is that why he was so grumpy last night?</i>

00:03:54.980 --> 00:03:56.710
<i>The thing worrying me the most is...</i>

00:03:56.710 --> 00:04:00.170
<i>when my sisters will return to normal.</i>

00:04:00.870 --> 00:04:05.140
<i>Given past experience, it won't 
last longer than 24 hours.</i>

00:04:05.140 --> 00:04:08.250
<i>It's already been 12 hours since last night.</i>

00:04:08.250 --> 00:04:10.360
<i>It could happen any minute...</i>

00:04:11.600 --> 00:04:14.370
<i>I've got plenty pills left, 
but want to avoid multiple doses,</i>

00:04:14.370 --> 00:04:17.690
<i>since they might aggravate the side effects.</i>

00:04:18.140 --> 00:04:19.190
Everyone!

00:04:19.190 --> 00:04:22.420
Would you guys like to go 
mountain climbing today?

00:04:22.420 --> 00:04:24.310
It seems like you went 
to the beach yesterday,

00:04:24.310 --> 00:04:26.280
so I thought the mountains for today!

00:04:26.280 --> 00:04:27.970
It's a good time of year for it, too.

00:04:27.970 --> 00:04:29.200
<i>Mountain climbing?</i>

00:04:29.200 --> 00:04:31.340
There are lots of unusual 
things in the mountains,

00:04:31.340 --> 00:04:33.960
and the view from the top is fantastic!

00:04:33.960 --> 00:04:37.250
<i>And if something went wrong, the girls 
could hide out in the mountains!</i>

00:04:37.250 --> 00:04:37.960
Fine by me.

00:04:38.290 --> 00:04:41.210
Yeah. We'll let Tani-chan decide.

00:04:41.210 --> 00:04:42.390
Let's go, then.

00:04:42.390 --> 00:04:43.510
Get ready, everyone.

00:04:43.510 --> 00:04:44.360
Okay!

00:04:45.620 --> 00:04:48.400
<i>These kids are kind of weird.</i>

00:04:48.400 --> 00:04:50.470
<i>The youngest is the leader?</i>

00:04:55.690 --> 00:04:58.690
A photosynthesis buffet!

00:05:04.280 --> 00:05:06.690
It's just an ordinary mountain path.

00:05:07.800 --> 00:05:10.340
<i>He must have been raised in 
a precipitous environment...</i>

00:05:09.590 --> 00:05:11.410
Ah, look!

00:05:12.740 --> 00:05:15.310
This tree is just like the one at our house!

00:05:15.310 --> 00:05:16.420
Let me see!

00:05:18.420 --> 00:05:21.710
<i>Aisuri-neesan seems pretty calm,</i>

00:05:21.710 --> 00:05:24.900
<i>but I think the dog in Snow-niisan 
has reached its limit.</i>

00:05:24.900 --> 00:05:28.590
When I'm in a wide-open space, 
my dog blood starts itching!

00:05:29.500 --> 00:05:31.670
Ashisu-neesan is having fun.

00:05:31.670 --> 00:05:36.020
But Aisuri isn't acting like herself...

00:05:36.340 --> 00:05:37.940
Not like herself?

00:05:37.030 --> 00:05:38.290
Let me have it!

00:05:38.290 --> 00:05:39.740
Just for a minute.

00:05:39.740 --> 00:05:41.110
Stop that!

00:05:41.110 --> 00:05:42.390
The poor thing...

00:05:42.390 --> 00:05:43.190
Shut up!

00:05:43.190 --> 00:05:44.890
It's Sumire-chan!

00:05:46.200 --> 00:05:48.760
Sumire-chan! What are you up to?

00:05:49.910 --> 00:05:50.950
Kanisu?

00:05:51.560 --> 00:05:53.000
Who's that?

00:05:53.000 --> 00:05:54.470
Tanisu's goddess.

00:05:54.470 --> 00:05:57.460
Oh, to be young again!

00:05:59.840 --> 00:06:01.820
What are you doing here?

00:06:01.820 --> 00:06:03.460
Who are they?

00:06:04.960 --> 00:06:06.190
They're my classmates.

00:06:06.190 --> 00:06:07.930
We're on a class trip here.

00:06:10.320 --> 00:06:11.350
I see...

00:06:13.770 --> 00:06:16.270
I told you to stop it!

00:06:20.080 --> 00:06:21.480
Spiders are beneficial insects!

00:06:21.480 --> 00:06:23.020
Leave it alone!

00:06:25.130 --> 00:06:26.030
Yeah!

00:06:26.030 --> 00:06:29.150
I don't care if they're 
useful! They're creepy!

00:06:29.460 --> 00:06:31.160
But...

00:06:31.770 --> 00:06:34.900
<i>What would Aisuri-neesan 
say if she heard that?</i>

00:06:35.450 --> 00:06:38.850
Hey kids, you shouldn't tease living things.

00:06:38.850 --> 00:06:43.500
If you do... it could become 
a monster and take revenge!

00:06:47.590 --> 00:06:48.510
That's dumb.

00:06:48.510 --> 00:06:50.660
<i>What little jerks!</i>

00:06:52.010 --> 00:06:54.330
These bugs are just creepy!

00:06:54.330 --> 00:06:56.150
Who cares if I kill a few?

00:06:56.150 --> 00:06:57.040
Stop!

00:07:05.710 --> 00:07:07.130
Aisuri-neesan?

00:07:07.730 --> 00:07:09.110
It's already dead.

00:07:11.890 --> 00:07:12.720
See?

00:07:15.870 --> 00:07:16.990
What are you doing?!

00:07:16.990 --> 00:07:19.500
What, you're not gonna eat it?

00:07:19.500 --> 00:07:21.840
Why'd you kill it, then?

00:07:21.840 --> 00:07:24.130
I didn't kill it!

00:07:24.480 --> 00:07:26.240
You damaged its web.

00:07:26.240 --> 00:07:28.420
It takes a lot of work to make.

00:07:32.160 --> 00:07:33.930
Humans are strange creatures.

00:07:33.930 --> 00:07:36.860
Aisuri-neesan! Don't do it here!

00:07:36.860 --> 00:07:39.730
You shouldn't waste food, though!

00:07:43.030 --> 00:07:45.290
Miss! Miss!

00:07:48.570 --> 00:07:49.690
What?

00:07:50.260 --> 00:07:53.050
Your hair is so pretty!

00:07:53.050 --> 00:07:55.200
It's slightly curly, like a foreign girl's!

00:07:58.090 --> 00:07:59.620
This is pretty?

00:08:00.120 --> 00:08:02.150
Yeah! Really pretty!

00:08:02.150 --> 00:08:03.650
Were you born with it that way?

00:08:05.430 --> 00:08:07.630
I don't wanna talk about it. Get lost.

00:08:07.630 --> 00:08:11.310
My big sister is very brave and kind,

00:08:11.310 --> 00:08:15.590
so God gave her beautiful hair as a reward.

00:08:15.590 --> 00:08:16.930
A reward.

00:08:16.930 --> 00:08:19.770
Then I'll protect Hikari-chan 
and Nozomi-chan!

00:08:19.770 --> 00:08:22.440
Me, too! I'll protect you, Aoi-chan!

00:08:22.440 --> 00:08:23.600
Me, too!

00:08:23.600 --> 00:08:26.120
This all sounds like you're making fun of me.

00:08:26.120 --> 00:08:27.610
It's true.

00:08:28.310 --> 00:08:31.110
Your hair is very beautiful, Aisuri.

00:08:31.110 --> 00:08:33.610
And you are courageous and kind.

00:08:36.980 --> 00:08:39.370
Stop talking like that.

00:08:45.040 --> 00:08:49.630
This stuff... it wasn't 
a gift from God at all.

00:08:50.900 --> 00:08:55.840
Aisuri, you yourself are a gift 
from God to the rest of us.

00:08:59.350 --> 00:09:01.780
Everyone, come over here!

00:09:03.750 --> 00:09:05.910
Okay, goodbye!

00:09:08.750 --> 00:09:10.110
Does it hurt?

00:09:10.110 --> 00:09:13.610
Allow me to apologize on their behalf. For...

00:09:15.450 --> 00:09:16.690
It's all right.

00:09:17.530 --> 00:09:20.020
I wish I could have saved it, though...

00:09:21.840 --> 00:09:24.420
Sumire-chan, come along now!

00:09:25.580 --> 00:09:27.790
She's calling you.

00:09:29.270 --> 00:09:30.670
R-Right!

00:09:34.710 --> 00:09:36.010
Okay, everyone!

00:09:36.430 --> 00:09:39.010
That's all wrapped up, so let's get going!

00:09:39.470 --> 00:09:41.810
We're almost to the goal!

00:09:45.870 --> 00:09:47.320
A windmill!

00:09:49.130 --> 00:09:50.350
In Netherlands...

00:09:50.350 --> 00:09:52.120
Sumire-chan's here, too!

00:09:55.410 --> 00:09:57.530
Hey, Sumire-chan!

00:09:58.780 --> 00:10:02.070
Okay! You're free to wander now.

00:10:02.070 --> 00:10:04.540
Make sure you know the time 
and place for the meet-up!

00:10:04.540 --> 00:10:05.570
Okay!

00:10:05.570 --> 00:10:09.540
Okay, let's go. We'll hit the windmill first.

00:10:11.000 --> 00:10:14.760
Sorry, can Snow-niisan go off on his own?

00:10:16.630 --> 00:10:18.760
You don't like windmills?

00:10:18.760 --> 00:10:21.040
Um...

00:10:22.140 --> 00:10:24.890
I think he's gonna poop his pants!

00:10:25.480 --> 00:10:26.980
R-Really?

00:10:26.980 --> 00:10:28.290
There's a bathroom up ahead.

00:10:28.290 --> 00:10:30.340
Be careful on the way back, okay?

00:10:30.340 --> 00:10:33.900
Great! Snow-niisan, you can 
put your clothes in there.

00:10:34.460 --> 00:10:37.610
What? He can't do it unless 
he takes off all his clothes?

00:10:42.640 --> 00:10:44.290
How pretty!

00:10:46.960 --> 00:10:50.810
<i>Getting to run around with 
Sumire-chan... it's just like a date!</i>

00:10:50.810 --> 00:10:52.470
<i>Maybe it </i>is<i> a date!</i>

00:10:55.130 --> 00:10:57.130
Look at that white doggy!

00:10:57.130 --> 00:10:59.000
Snow-niisan!

00:10:59.930 --> 00:11:02.590
I see your classmates from before, too...

00:11:02.590 --> 00:11:04.470
Oh, yeah!

00:11:04.470 --> 00:11:08.890
Hey, John! Don't write our names there!

00:11:08.890 --> 00:11:13.360
It's good luck. It'll let us 
stay together forever.

00:11:14.150 --> 00:11:17.150
<i>What would Ashisu-neesan 
think if she saw this?</i>

00:11:26.330 --> 00:11:29.580
Oh, is that man with the 
white hair your brother?

00:11:30.940 --> 00:11:32.580
Yeah, that's Snow-niisan.

00:11:32.580 --> 00:11:34.930
<i>He seemed nice!</i>

00:11:34.930 --> 00:11:36.800
<i>What is it, Sumire?</i>

00:11:45.430 --> 00:11:46.930
This wind...

00:11:47.660 --> 00:11:49.330
It feels great.

00:11:51.930 --> 00:11:53.720
Reading minds, like Suishi?

00:11:53.720 --> 00:11:55.940
It's known as "thought transference."

00:11:59.940 --> 00:12:02.350
We look so different...

00:12:03.110 --> 00:12:07.030
...but we are unquestionably twins.

00:12:10.790 --> 00:12:12.070
Aisuri?

00:12:16.460 --> 00:12:18.450
And then, Ashisu-neesan said—

00:12:19.050 --> 00:12:20.260
Tanisu.

00:12:20.260 --> 00:12:23.130
Ashisu-neesan went running 
after Aisuri-neesan.

00:12:25.000 --> 00:12:25.840
The time has come.

00:12:27.180 --> 00:12:29.310
I'm off! You handle things here!

00:12:31.360 --> 00:12:33.230
What's with him?

00:12:35.270 --> 00:12:36.560
He needs the bathroom, perhaps.

00:12:37.450 --> 00:12:39.940
<i>Was there a problem with my breakfast?</i>

00:12:45.950 --> 00:12:49.450
<i>I told them to hide in the mountains 
if the medicine started wearing off!</i>

00:13:00.390 --> 00:13:02.260
Wait, Aisuri!

00:13:04.220 --> 00:13:05.360
Stay back!

00:13:10.970 --> 00:13:13.480
Run away while you can still move.

00:13:14.200 --> 00:13:15.480
I can't!

00:13:18.480 --> 00:13:21.110
I might eat you!

00:13:27.100 --> 00:13:27.990
Stupid.

00:13:28.760 --> 00:13:30.510
I'm...

00:13:32.060 --> 00:13:34.000
the same way you are...

00:13:42.590 --> 00:13:44.380
Dammit!

00:13:44.380 --> 00:13:48.640
<i>When I was little, I convinced 
myself it was just a bad dream.</i>

00:13:58.030 --> 00:14:00.610
<i>But it wasn't a dream.</i>

00:14:06.360 --> 00:14:08.470
<i>Ashisu and I are twins.</i>

00:14:09.200 --> 00:14:12.870
<i>We're a little different, 
but we really are twins.</i>

00:14:23.430 --> 00:14:25.090
Ron.

00:14:25.090 --> 00:14:27.550
You searching for spiders again?

00:14:27.550 --> 00:14:30.260
I don't have to search for 
spiders to find them!

00:14:31.760 --> 00:14:32.740
Look!

00:14:41.250 --> 00:14:43.960
<i>No! Aisuri, don't do it!</i>

00:14:44.890 --> 00:14:46.440
Mama!

00:14:46.770 --> 00:14:48.780
Can you tell which is which?

00:14:50.420 --> 00:14:54.280
Oh, please. You're totally different.

00:14:54.280 --> 00:14:56.310
That's not true.

00:14:57.120 --> 00:14:59.790
Compare our hairstyles!

00:15:01.050 --> 00:15:03.290
Compare our eyes!

00:15:05.030 --> 00:15:07.460
Compare our shadows!

00:15:08.870 --> 00:15:13.680
Yes, the more you grow, 
the more alike you seem to look.

00:15:13.680 --> 00:15:17.960
We could have filmed a superhero movie 
about a spider-woman and a plant-woman.

00:15:19.110 --> 00:15:21.360
What's a movie?

00:15:22.180 --> 00:15:25.690
You don't need to know such things.

00:15:32.120 --> 00:15:34.870
Help!

00:15:35.200 --> 00:15:36.850
Over here!

00:15:44.210 --> 00:15:45.210
Run!

00:15:52.410 --> 00:15:54.600
<i>My body is hardening up.</i>

00:15:54.600 --> 00:15:56.060
<i>I don't have much time...</i>

00:15:56.060 --> 00:15:57.060
<i>Tani-chan!</i>

00:16:16.690 --> 00:16:19.080
<i>I can't let her reach a populated area.</i>

00:16:19.080 --> 00:16:20.500
<i>So...</i>

00:18:03.930 --> 00:18:09.940
<b>Frankenstein Extras!</b>

00:18:04.810 --> 00:18:06.630
<i>Frankenstein Extras!</i>

00:18:07.790 --> 00:18:09.940
<b>Today's theme is...</b>

00:18:07.790 --> 00:18:09.940
<i>Today's theme is...</i>

00:18:09.940 --> 00:18:17.190
I'm Yuuyu, and I'm in charge of the 
background music for <i>Frankenstein Family</i>.

00:18:10.580 --> 00:18:18.990
<b>Yuuyu
 Composer (Background Music) for <i>Frankenstein Family</i></b>

00:18:17.190 --> 00:18:18.990
A pleasure to meet you.

00:18:36.650 --> 00:18:39.470
<b>What did you think when you were
 put in charge of the music?</b>

00:18:39.470 --> 00:18:45.010
When they first proposed it, I found 
it to be a very curious work.

00:18:41.320 --> 00:18:53.440
<b>*Face not shown at subject's request</b>

00:18:45.010 --> 00:18:48.610
It's not the kind of story I read very often.

00:18:48.610 --> 00:18:51.800
I thought about it from several 
directions, about how to approach it,

00:18:51.800 --> 00:18:53.440
before starting up.

00:18:53.440 --> 00:18:59.820
I'd done opening and ending themes 
for various anime in the past,

00:18:59.820 --> 00:19:02.070
but this was my first time doing BGM.

00:19:02.070 --> 00:19:07.000
An opening theme has to sort of 
summarize the show as a whole.

00:19:07.000 --> 00:19:08.620
So you want to do something

00:19:08.620 --> 00:19:11.700
that really impresses on
 people what the show is like.

00:19:11.700 --> 00:19:16.670
There were more things I had to adapt 
to scene by scene in the moment.

00:19:16.670 --> 00:19:20.050
It was nerve-wracking, but I gave it my best.

00:19:20.240 --> 00:19:23.050
<b>What's the most important 
part of the music?</b>

00:19:23.050 --> 00:19:25.840
It shouldn't be too dispassionate,

00:19:25.840 --> 00:19:29.940
but you also don't want drastic 
developments coming out of nowhere.

00:19:29.940 --> 00:19:33.900
It's a work that proceeds 
with a very curious tone.

00:19:33.900 --> 00:19:38.990
Given what they told me, I decided 
to go with mainly piano,

00:19:38.990 --> 00:19:45.220
but then add or take away 
instruments where appropriate.

00:19:45.220 --> 00:19:51.660
The "family" part of the work is very strong,
 so I wanted to express that with music.

00:19:51.660 --> 00:19:56.410
The melodies are mostly similar, 
but the accompaniment changes,

00:19:56.410 --> 00:20:01.140
and I apply the same motifs 
differently into various songs.

00:20:01.140 --> 00:20:03.990
It gives you a different atmosphere 
in different locations.

00:20:03.990 --> 00:20:07.790
It brings a feeling of family 
to the whole work.

00:20:07.790 --> 00:20:11.310
I hope people enjoy that part of it.

00:20:11.540 --> 00:20:14.350
<b>What's your personal favorite song?</b>

00:20:14.350 --> 00:20:17.830
I've composed a few dozen
 songs for the show,

00:20:17.830 --> 00:20:23.710
but there's a song that 
communicates "determination"...

00:20:23.710 --> 00:20:30.800
It starts off soft, and as you get to the 
second half, it suddenly gets louder,

00:20:30.800 --> 00:20:35.030
and the melody develops, too.

00:20:35.030 --> 00:20:38.060
It's a very melodious piece.

00:20:38.060 --> 00:20:42.730
I think it was my favorite piece 
to compose. I really like it.

00:20:47.700 --> 00:21:56.960
<b>Song that expresses "Determination"</b>

00:21:56.960 --> 00:22:00.150
<b>Who is your favorite character
 in <i>Frankenstein Family</i>?</b>

00:22:00.080 --> 00:22:08.710
<b>Who is your favorite character
 in <i>Frankenstein Family</i>?</b>

00:22:00.530 --> 00:22:05.450
Let's see. All the characters are unique.

00:22:05.450 --> 00:22:08.720
They all reject the typical cliches.

00:22:08.720 --> 00:22:13.240
But personally, I like Snow-niisan,

00:22:13.240 --> 00:22:19.590
both for his personality and the 
fact that he's merged with a dog.

00:22:19.590 --> 00:22:21.500
I always liked animals,

00:22:21.500 --> 00:22:25.120
so the way he'll turn into a dog on a dime

00:22:25.120 --> 00:22:27.070
is something I really like.

00:22:30.710 --> 00:22:32.450
Hey, you dumb mutt!

00:22:33.080 --> 00:22:36.270
My dog side doesn't handle 
this atmosphere well,

00:22:36.270 --> 00:22:38.580
and I've always wanted to try chopsticks...

00:22:38.960 --> 00:22:41.670
This is much harder than I imagined it to be!

00:22:42.160 --> 00:22:44.420
Tanisu does it so well...

00:22:44.550 --> 00:22:47.420
<b>Give a message to our viewers!</b>

00:22:47.420 --> 00:22:52.790
There are a lot more developments 
to come in <i>Frankenstein Family</i>.

00:22:52.790 --> 00:22:56.860
How will Tanisu's feelings develop?

00:22:56.860 --> 00:23:00.520
What will happen to the 
family and the siblings?

00:23:00.520 --> 00:23:02.770
I'm really looking forward to it.

